### Teste dos endpoints de logout e unbind no FireBirdAPI
### Este arquivo testa o fluxo completo no FireBirdAPI (API local)

### 1. Primeiro, fazer login para obter um token
POST http://localhost:5000/api/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2. Registrar um nó anônimo
POST http://localhost:5000/api/Auth/anonymous/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Node",
  "machineId": "TEST-MACHINE-001",
  "ipAddress": "192.168.1.100",
  "port": 8080,
  "databasePath": "C:\\Test\\database.fdb",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "operatingSystem": "Windows 10"
}

### 3. Vincular o nó anônimo ao usuário (usar o token do login e anonymousToken do registro)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/Auth/bind-node
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "anonymousToken": "{{anonymousToken}}"
}

### 4. Verificar nós do usuário (deve mostrar o nó vinculado)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/Auth/nodes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Desvincular um nó específico
POST http://localhost:5000/api/Auth/unbind-node
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "nodeId": "{{nodeId}}"
}

### 6. Fazer logout (apenas registra o logout, não desvincula nós)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/Auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Tentar acessar nós do usuário após logout (deve retornar 401)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/Auth/nodes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
